# X6.2b: response headers for the static front at the final edge (Cloudflare static assets / Pages read this file from
# the build output; Vite copies public/ there unchanged). The page also sets the same policy itself (index.html
# <meta name="referrer">), so it holds on a host that ignores this file.
#
# Referrer-Policy is strict-origin-when-cross-origin, deliberately NOT no-referrer or same-origin: under those two, a
# browser sends `Origin: null` on a non-CORS POST (Fetch "append a request Origin header"), e.g. the invitation SSO form
# POST to the API (features/auth/AcceptInvitation.tsx) or any POST through a same-origin /rest proxy, and the API's
# Origin-only CSRF checks (cookie-csrf.util.ts) refuse `null`. strict-origin-when-cross-origin keeps the real Origin,
# and a cross-origin Referer carries the origin only: never a path or query string (XA-08: the forgot-password
# address in the URL never reaches a third party such as the font host).
/*
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
